    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "属性断言：Equations (3.68), (3.72), and (3.73) characterize the transient response of a system having no finite zeros and two complex poles and with undamped natural frequency ω_n, damping ratio ζ, and negative real part σ. In analysis and design, they are used to estimate rise time, overshoot, and settling time, respectively, for just about any system.",
